<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Ile Sainte-Marie</h1><p class="st-meta">1750 CE – 1896 CE · capital Ambodifotatra</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An island off Madagascar's east coast that went from pirate haven to French outpost, ceded to France in 1750.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the 1690s Ile Sainte-Marie (Nosy Boraha) became a base for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> raiding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, with a trading post run by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adam-baldridge">Adam Baldridge</a> supplying them. Descendants of the pirates and local Malagasy later formed part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/betsimisaraka-confederation">Betsimisaraka Confederation</a>. In 1750 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princess-bety">Princess Bety</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratsimilaho">Ratsimilaho</a>, ceded the island to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-east-india-company">French East India Company</a> established a small post, but disease and a Malagasy uprising soon forced its abandonment. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> reoccupied the island in 1818 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sylvain-roux">Sylvain Roux</a>, building at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambodifotatra">Ambodifotatra</a> a base for trade and for French claims on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. It was administered from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ile-bourbon">Ile Bourbon</a> for much of the 19th century, with a small Catholic population.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1896 Sainte-Marie was attached to the new French colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, and it has been part of Madagascar since independence in 1960.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1750 CE – 1896 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.53%;width:2.91%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1750 CE – 1896 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ambodifotatra</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sylvain Roux</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity, traditional Malagasy religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French, Malagasy</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nosy Boraha, Sainte-Marie</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1823&amp;focus=ile-sainte-marie" aria-label="Ile Sainte-Marie on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6037 2805 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ile Sainte-Marie lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6357 3061L5054 728M6357 3061L6286 3134"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M6286 3134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6357 3061h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6357 3061h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1823&amp;focus=ile-sainte-marie">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
